RangeForce: Password Spraying

Platform: RangeForce  
Room: Password Spraying  
Difficulty: Advanced
Date: 2026  

Objective  
Learn how password spraying attacks are conducted using automated tools and how they can be detected and mitigated. The goal was to understand how attackers attempt to gain access to multiple accounts using common passwords while avoiding account lockouts.

Step 1: Understanding Password Spraying  
I began by learning how password spraying differs from traditional brute-force attacks. Instead of attempting many passwords against a single account, password spraying uses one or a few common passwords across many accounts to reduce the likelihood of triggering lockout mechanisms.

Step 2: Executing a Password Spray with Hydra  
Next, I used Hydra to perform a password spraying attack against multiple user accounts. Hydra automated authentication attempts by applying a single password across a list of usernames, demonstrating how attackers can efficiently test credentials at scale.

This step highlighted how easily weak or reused passwords can be exploited in environments without strong authentication controls.

Step 3: Analyzing Results and Impact  
After executing the attack, I analyzed the results to identify any successful logins. This demonstrated how attackers can discover valid credentials with minimal noise, making password spraying a stealthy and effective technique.

Conclusion & Outcome  
Through this exercise, I gained hands-on experience performing password spraying attacks using Hydra. This reinforced the importance of strong password policies, account lockout configurations, and multi-factor authentication to defend against credential-based attacks.

